direction: down

title: |md
  ### Neighbour output: unresolved queue, stale validation, and two fast paths
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

tx: "TX has a next-hop neighbour" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  t_body: |md
    ip_finish_output2 reaches:

    `neigh_output(neigh, skb, skip_cache)`

    It first tests connected state + hh cache.
    Otherwise it calls the current
    `neigh->output` function pointer.
  |
}

unresolved: "NONE / INCOMPLETE: resolve" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  u_body: |md
    `neigh_resolve_output()` calls
    `__neigh_event_send()`.

    NONE → INCOMPLETE
    arm timer + send ARP solicitation

    Return 1: this skb is not transmitted now.
  |
}

queue: "Bounded arp_queue" {
  style.fill: "#ede9fe"
  q_body: |md
    Only INCOMPLETE traffic is parked here.

    Limit is bytes (`QUEUE_LEN_BYTES`).
    If the new skb would overflow it,
    dequeue/drop oldest entries until it fits:
    `SKB_DROP_REASON_NEIGH_QUEUEFULL`.
  |
}

reply: "ARP reply: neighbour becomes REACHABLE" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  r_body: |md
    neigh_update stores the MAC.
    neigh_connect selects connected output.

    Queue drain relooks up the top-level
    neighbour for each skb, then reinjects it.
  |
}

hh: "Fast path A: neigh_hh_output" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  h_body: |md
    If state is NUD_CONNECTED and `hh_len` exists,
    the inline helper bypasses `neigh->output`:

    copy cached L2 header under seqlock
    push header → dev_queue_xmit
  |
}

connected: "Fast path B: connected_output" {
  style.fill: "#fff7ed"
  c_body: |md
    Without a usable header cache, fall through
    to the function pointer.

    Generic `neigh_connected_output()` calls
    dev_hard_header for this skb, then transmits.

    This is an alternative to the hh-cache path.
  |
}

stale: "STALE: send now, validate later" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  s_body: |md
    neigh_suspect selects resolving output.

    Next packet changes STALE → DELAY but
    `__neigh_event_send()` returns success;
    the known MAC is used immediately.

    No upper-layer confirmation by timer expiry?
    DELAY → PROBE and solicitations begin.
    STALE traffic is not queued.
  |
}

fail: "Resolution failure" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  f_body: |md
    Probe budget exhausted while INCOMPLETE:
    state → FAILED

    queued skbs pass through error_report;
    IPv4 calls dst_link_failure and frees them
    with NEIGH_FAILED accounting.
  |
}

tx -> unresolved: "address not usable"
unresolved -> queue: "INCOMPLETE: park skb"
queue -> reply: "reply before probe budget expires"
queue -> fail: "no reply"
reply -> hh: "connected + cached header"
reply -> connected: "connected, no usable hh cache"
tx -> stale: "known MAC, stale reachability"
stale -> connected: "send current packet"
